<html>
<head>
<style>
  body { font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; padding: 16px; }
  h2 { color: #333; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  h3 { color: #555; margin-top: 16px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8px 0; }
  td, th { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px 10px; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #f0f0f0; }
  .section { margin-bottom: 24px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h2>Trace Test: [%=network.people.size()%] People</h2>

[** ===== TEST 1: Basic trace(value) - auto-detected element/property ===== **]
<div class="section">
  <h3>1. Basic trace(value)</h3>
  <p>Each name below should be independently traceable (hover for toolbar):</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Person</th><th>Traced Name</th></tr>
    [%for (p in network.people) {%]
    <tr>
      <td>[%=p.name%]</td>
      <td>[%=trace(p.name, Sequence{"show", "edit"})%]</td>
    </tr>
    [%}%]
  </table>
</div>

[** ===== TEST 2: Multiple traces in the same element ===== **]
<div class="section">
  <h3>2. Multiple traces per element</h3>
  <p>Two traced values inside the same &lt;span&gt; — each should highlight independently:</p>
  [%for (p in network.people) {%]
  [%  if (p.likes.size() > 0) { var liked = p.likes.first(); %]
  <p><b>[%=trace(p.name, Sequence{"show", "edit"})%]</b> likes <b>[%=trace(liked.name, Sequence{"show"})%]</b></p>
  [%  } %]
  [%}%]
</div>

[** ===== TEST 3: trace(value, allowedActions) — filtered actions ===== **]
<div class="section">
  <h3>3. Trace with filtered actions</h3>
  <p>Only "show" action should appear (no "edit"):</p>
  <ul>
  [%for (p in network.people) {%]
    <li>Show only: [%=trace(p.name, Sequence{"show"})%]</li>
  [%}%]
  </ul>
</div>

[** ===== TEST 4: trace(value, element, allowedActions) — explicit element ===== **]
<div class="section">
  <h3>4. Trace with explicit element</h3>
  <p>Name traced against a different element (the network itself):</p>
  [%var firstPerson = network.people.first();%]
  <p>Person name "[%=trace(firstPerson.name, network, Sequence{"show", "edit"})%]" traced to the SocialNetwork element</p>
</div>

[** ===== TEST 5: Non-traced text (negative test) ===== **]
<div class="section">
  <h3>5. Non-traced text (no toolbar expected)</h3>
  <p>These are plain values — hovering should show NO toolbar:</p>
  <ul>
  [%for (p in network.people) {%]
    <li>[%=p.name%]</li>
  [%}%]
  </ul>
</div>

[** ===== TEST 6: Traced text in nested HTML ===== **]
<div class="section">
  <h3>6. Traced text inside nested HTML</h3>
  <p>Traces inside table cells, list items, and bold/italic:</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Person</th><th>Likes</th><th>Dislikes</th></tr>
    [%for (p in network.people) {%]
    <tr>
      <td><b>[%=trace(p.name, Sequence{"show", "edit"})%]</b></td>
      <td>[%=p.likes.collect(l|trace(l.name, Sequence{"show"})).concat(", ")%]</td>
      <td>[%=p.dislikes.collect(d|trace(d.name, Sequence{"show"})).concat(", ")%]</td>
    </tr>
    [%}%]
  </table>
</div>

</body>
</html>
